s70_inout run log [P] single engine, own rules, not yet two-engine.  No bounds claimed: every K LP value below is a transient pointer on a partial row set.
Base: s69_rrzq7 (copied: eng/, env69.sh -> env70.sh, runK69.sh -> runK70.sh, warm0_rows.txt, tab/).  s69/s67/s64/s60 untouched.
Change: in-out (stabilised) separation in the K loop.  eng/pinout.py (helpers + options) and eng/prelay2.py (cmd_solveR2: the post-LP part is now the nested function sepround(xv, t, tail, dry); driver chooses the point).
  inout=lam0,lam1,step : separate at x_sep = lam*x_LP + (1-lam)*x_feas (all LP columns keyed as in the sol json, t and y included; x_feas = sol_feas.json = sol_c_repaired_opusfmt.json with rr/z/zr/q at 0, FEASIBLE at t=0.041565 on keep95p131f).
     lam starts at lam0; raised by step (cap lam1) when a blended round finds nothing or < inoutmin (30) new rows; if lam1 is reached and nothing is found, a RAW (lam=1) separation (with the d>17 tail/Karp part) is done.
  inoutk=k (4)         : every k-th iteration (it+1)%k==0 a raw separation is done instead (its cuts are added too).  Convergence (the keeppen stop) can only trigger when a raw separation finds nothing.
  feas=<json>          : the feasible point.   inoutctl=lam [rawsol=json] : dry-run control (no LP, no warm).
  Only valid rows are ever added (rows come from the separator); the blend only chooses where to look.
Controls (logs/ctl_*.log, ctl70.sh):  lam=0 on keep95p131f: t_sep=0.041565, 0/22476 sender rows violated, 0 conservation rows violated, 0 receiver violations d=7..17 (exhaustive up to K=300/d) -> PASS.
  lam=1 (raw = sol_rrz_rand.json): blended vector bit-identical to the raw one (asserted), 300/d violations (capped) = what the old loop sees.  lam=0.4 on the same raw point: max excess scales ~0.4 (3.3 vs 8.8 at d=7), 300/d.
